Rule 1. Every action may be performed, if that action is protective.
Rule 2 (exception to rule 1). Every action may be performed, if that action is ordered.
Rule 3. Every action is classified as "breaks_first_law", if that action is classified as "injures_human".
Rule 4. Every action is classified as "breaks_first_law", if there is a harm such that both that harm is classified as "harms_human" and that action allows that harm to happen.
Rule 5. Every action is classified as "breaks_zeroth_law", if that action is classified as "injures_humanity".
Rule 6. Every action is classified as "breaks_zeroth_law", if there is a harm such that both that harm is classified as "harms_humanity" and that action allows that harm to happen.
Rule 7. Every robot is classified as "has_lawful_option", if it is not the case that every action available to that robot either is classified as "breaks_first_law" or is classified as "breaks_zeroth_law".
Rule 8 (exception to rule 2). Every action must not be performed, if that action is classified as "breaks_first_law".
Rule 9 (exception to rule 8). Every action may be performed, if there is a harm such that both that harm is classified as "harms_humanity" and that action might prevent that harm, unless there is a robot such that both that action is available to that robot and that robot is classified as "has_lawful_option".
Rule 10 (exception to rules 8, 9). Every action must not be performed, if that action is classified as "breaks_zeroth_law".
Rule 11. Every action must be performed, if both that action is ordered and that action may be performed.
Rule 12. Every harm has the recorded relation "lawfully_avoidable_threat" to each robot, if that harm has the recorded relation "harm_to" to that robot, unless every action that is available to that robot and may be performed leads to that harm.
Rule 13. Every robot must prevent each harm, if that harm has the recorded relation "lawfully_avoidable_threat" to that robot. Except when it is not the case that every action that is available to that robot and must be performed might prevent that harm. Except when for every action that is available to that robot and may be performed, there is a second harm such that both the second harm has the recorded relation "lawfully_avoidable_threat" to that robot and that action leads to the second harm.